-------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
[TXT] Don't Relocate SACM if no LLC

[Issue Description]
ACHECK ACM launch was failing with UCODE error on 0+0+4 config.
Turns out that if no LLC, then relocating ACM from flash location is
not an option.
Before ACM launch, UCODE loads ACM to MLC from level higher in mem
(generally LLC).
In MLC-only case, there is no LLC. Level higher is SPI flash.
Since SPI flash at alternate location (ie TempRAM) does not contain ACM,
GETSEC[ENTERACCS] launch would fail with UCODE error

[Resolution]
If no LLC, then must use an MTRR to cover ACM at flash location.

